  "plan": {
    "goal": "Co-incubate UGT2B7 with testosterone at 2771.1 µM in the presence of a competitive inhibitor and quantify the inhibitor:substrate ratio, percent inhibition, and run-condition IC50.",
    "rationale": "UGT2B7 glucuronidation of testosterone (substrate) is modeled as a Michaelis-Menten reaction with competitive inhibition. Km = 1982.4 µM, [S] = 2771.1 µM, Ki = 207.4 µM, [I] = 319.8 µM, Vmax = 1.8388 µmol/min. The fractional activity under competitive inhibition is v_i/v_0 = [S]/(Km(1+[I]/Ki)+[S]); percent inhibition = (1 - fractional activity) x 100. Run-condition IC50 follows Cheng-Prusoff: IC50 = Ki(1+[S]/Km). Inhibitor:substrate molar ratio = [I]/[S].",
